<#
Add-Instructor-Dummy-Data.ps1

Populates dummy/demo data across the Instructor portal pages that were
previously showing empty arrays or hardcoded zero/dash KPI values:
  - instructor/courses      (My Courses list)
  - instructor/reviews      (Reviews + replies)
  - instructor/students     (Students list)
  - instructor/promotions   (Course dropdown + active promotions list)
  - instructor/dashboard    (KPI cards + recent reviews)
  - instructor/analytics    (KPI cards)
  - instructor/earnings     (KPI cards + per-course earnings breakdown)

Each file is embedded below as Base64 and written directly into the
$files hashtable, then decoded with [System.IO.File]::WriteAllBytes().
No intermediate $b64_<name> variables are used, so there is no risk of
PowerShell mis-parsing a dot in a variable name (the bug from the
previous version of this script). This script itself is pure ASCII.

Run from the SAI2 project root:
    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\Add-Instructor-Dummy-Data.ps1
#>

$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"

$root = $PSScriptRoot
if (-not $root) { $root = (Get-Location).Path }

Write-Host "Project root: $root" -ForegroundColor Cyan

$files = @{}

